cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "scPerturbModel: context-dependent models of single-cell drug perturbation response on Tahoe-100M"
abstract: >-
  Analysis and modelling framework for the Tahoe-100M single-cell perturbation
  atlas: paper replication probes, must-beat baselines, context-residual and
  conditional-VAE response models, generalization benchmarks (held-out
  condition / cell line / drug, few-shot transfer), and an independent
  cell-type identity audit of the atlas cell lines against Tabula Sapiens.
